  "summary": "A fairly common resident, and nomadic. A small courser with a rufous cap, a rufous lower breast, a white belly and white legs. The immature is speckled buff on the upper parts and crown. It may call a sharp err-err-err in flight. It stands erect, runs, and sometimes bobs its head and tail. The Kemp code VB was left unchanged.",
